{
  "original_id": "newwin-00001-p06",
  "archive_id": "BW2-N01-P06",
  "title": "A first counterexample to the Archer-Bourne recurrence for the avoidance chain (312,54321:132)",
  "batch_label": "新WIN-1批次",
  "kind": "resolution-paper",
  "original_status": "disproved",
  "scope": "Let C_n be the permutations pi in S_n avoiding the classical subsequence patterns 312 and 54321 such that the composition square pi^2 avoids 132, and let a_n=|C_n| with a_0=1. Then (a_0,...,a_11)=(1,1,2,5,11,22,45,89,174,338,655,1265). The recurrence a_n=a_(n-1)+a_(n-2)+a_(n-3)+a_(n-4)+n-1 holds for 6<=n<=10 and first fails at n=11, where its right-hand side is 1266 instead of 1265. Thus the universally quantified original claim is false. The computer-assisted proof uses the complete nine-member classification of C_11 permutations ending in 1, the exact endpoint census through 11, and a proved direct-sum reduction; it makes no claim about a corrected all-n recurrence.",
  "gate_basis": "Current released terminal, manifest, PDF, TeX freeze, snapshot files, provenance and four audits agree.",
